      "text": "Metrication in the United States\nWine is sold in standard bottles of 750 mL , as in the rest of the world . A fifth of liquor , once one - fifth of a U.S. gallon , or 757 mL , is now commonly 750 mL , though it is still referred to as `` a fifth '' . Beer is sold in fluid ounce denominations . Regulations are set by the Alcohol and Tobacco Tax and Trade Bureau which controls the permissible sizes of containers . Unlike non-alcoholic beverages , most alcohol products are not required to carry unit conversions on labels . Tomatoes",
